+* `.ruby-version`, both Gemfiles/lockfiles, and CI use Ruby 3.4.8 / the 3.4 series.
+  `bigdecimal` is explicitly bundled now that Ruby 3.4 no longer supplies it as
+  a default gem. Roadie Rails 3.4 permits Rails 8.1; SQLite 2.x meets the new
+  adapter requirement and is also supported by 7.2. SQL Server adapters follow
+  their selected Rails series. Database schema and stored data are unchanged.
+* Wiki-history text duplicates uncompressed database strings before changing
+  encoding (SQLite 2.x may return frozen strings). Locale-option strings are
+  copied before encoding changes, avoiding Ruby 3.4 symbol-string warnings.
+* The controller `model_object` DSL uses a separate backing class attribute,
+  preserving getter/setter and inheritance semantics under Rails 8.1 (whose
+  attribute setters no longer redefine the public reader).
+* Randomized form names (the existing Firefox autofill workaround) are added
+  during HTML option construction, since newer form helpers bypass
+  `form_tag_html`. Explicit names and normal form rendering remain intact.
+* Rails 8.1 encodes nil query values as bare keys instead of `key=`. Redirect
